<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 1, unfitted field) (Dionaea muscipula)",
        "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 1, unfitted field) faithfully reproduces Dionaea muscipula morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dionaea muscipula specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Dionaea muscipula" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That a second assessor scored this audit.",
        "does_not_claim: That the pass-1 GIF is a pixel fit to the trap photograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.10, 0.90) and diffusivities that place λ_c at the assigned 24 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Semi-implicit Fourier integration of the nonlinear PDE on the 192 µm patch (--emit 1).",
        "reported_in_source: Forterre et al. 2005: the Dionaea lobe snaps by curvature inversion. That is context, not this wavelength law.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a linear reaction-diffusion system selects a finite critical wavenumber k_c.",
        "transfer_boundary: 24 µm is the slot scale (tier 4_cellular_10um, detail), not a new measurement of gland spacing.",
        "transfer_boundary: Age is 0 Ma, Holocene extant, chronoseries 1/1." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; output: docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Dionaea muscipula; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a linear reaction-diffusion system selects a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v. | Forterre et al. 2005: the Dionaea lobe snaps by curvature inversion. That is context, not this wavelength law.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.10, 0.90) and diffusivities that place λ_c at the assigned 24 µm. | Semi-implicit Fourier integration of the nonlinear PDE on the 192 µm patch (--emit 1).; transfer_boundary: 24 µm is the slot scale (tier 4_cellular_10um, detail), not a new measurement of gland spacing. | Age is 0 Ma, Holocene extant, chronoseries 1/1.; does_not_claim: That the pass-1 GIF is a pixel fit to the trap photograph. | That a second assessor scored this audit.]; phenomenon_size: 6.1 mm (0.006138 m, log10=-2.212 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 6.1 mm to 6.1 mm): 6.1 mm:venus-flytrap-snap-buckling" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03185>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-1> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Reaction-Diffusion & Turing Dispersion" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.94e-01 .

